%% tengri canonical citation database.
%%
%% This file is the SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for every citation registered in
%% tengri.citations. Python code parses this file at import time and builds
%% the REGISTRY dict from it. Do not hard-code citation data in Python —
%% add or edit entries here.
%%
%% Every entry below is sourced from an authoritative ADS BibTeX export
%% (copied from the tengri Paper I bibliography), not written from memory.
%%
%% Custom fields (non-standard BibTeX but accepted by our parser):
%%   registry_key   — the short key used by tengri.cite(registry_key)
%%   short          — one-line display string ("Author et al. (Year)")
%%   role           — human-readable description of what tengri uses this for
%%   upstream_code  — the URL path (e.g. "bd-j/prospector") when we port code
%%
%% Standard fields beyond ADS default set (doi, archivePrefix, eprint) are
%% preserved verbatim.
%%
%% See also:
%%   CITATION.bib at the repo root — the tengri papers (Paper I/II/III)
%%   VERIFICATION.md — component-to-paper verification status

